Read `.agents/conventions/service.md`. For replication work also read
`.agents/skills/peer-replication/SKILL.md`.

Handlers are pure functions taking `(payload, deps)` and returning a dict; they
never raise across the wire. All SQL lives in `store.py`. RNS is reached only
through the existing seams so tests need no sockets. Every op except
`__manifest__` requires `v == 1`. Signature verification is standalone first
(embedded pubkey, hash-bound to the identity field) then `Identity.recall`;
`Identity.load_public_key` returns None on success, so judge by `ident.hash`.
Peer-facing queries exclude attested records. Degrade rather than fail: no
Beacon database means registered-only answers.
